    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.86"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Demographic matrices directly estimate growth potential and realized limitation across many plants and animals. The universal wording exceeds coverage, but the central mechanism has clear and broadly testable consequences." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Compare potential population growth from fecundity and survival schedules with observed long-run abundance, and quantify density-, enemy- or environment-dependent mortality. Potential production exceeding realized recruitment with limiting mortality supports the mechanism." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Microbes and many invertebrates are underrepresented.", "'Struggle' requires mapping to measurable density dependence or mortality." ;
